# Cited patterns only

`docs/patterns.md` is the closed catalog of design patterns, architectural styles, and practices this project may use. Each entry cites its source.

Do not coin a pattern name. Do not add a pattern, library convention, or "best practice" that the catalog does not already cite.

To introduce one:

1. Add the citation (author, title, year, and URL when one exists) to `docs/patterns.md`.
2. Record why this codebase needs it in a new ADR under `docs/adr/`.
3. Name the packages it applies to.

`docs/architecture.md` must stay consistent with the catalog. If a prompt and the catalog disagree, stop and update the ADR first.

```text
Bad:  type SmartFolderBrain struct{} // unnamed, uncited
Good: type LibraryRepository interface{} // Repository, Evans 2003; see docs/patterns.md
```
